{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event is a value conforming to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" is a value: tracking an event records it as an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", with its timestamp, the caller’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SourceLocation"},{"type":"text","text":" and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":", as one of the tracker’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"records"},{"type":"text","text":". Delivering is a chain of operators over that sequence: Afluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch(strategy:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"type":"text","text":", the default) gathers the records into batches, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" hands each batch to every destination, as a lazy unit of work. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Destination"},{"type":"text","text":" is a plain sink, narrowed or transformed by its modifiers: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepting(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"droppingCallSite()"},{"type":"text","text":". A tracker given a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Consent"},{"type":"text","text":" delivers an event only once the user grants its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ConsentCategory"},{"type":"text","text":", holding it while undecided and dropping it when denied. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"type":"text","text":" only queues an event, from any thread; a worker the tracker owns, never on the main actor, does the rest. A tracker given a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":" writes each record to disk as its worker reaches it and delivers what an earlier run left first. A property whose valid values are narrower than its type is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refined"},{"type":"text","text":" value, which satisfies its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Refinement"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Constraint"},{"type":"text","text":"s from the moment it is made, or carries constraints declared with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"type":"text","text":"; the tracker’s worker rejects an event that breaks one before anything else, reporting each as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RejectionReport"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rejectionReports"},{"type":"text","text":". On Apple platforms, SwiftUI views read the tracker from the environment and track what they do with view modifiers, and a screen’s events carry its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenKey"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). UIKit views and view controllers inherit it as a trait, the same value as SwiftUI’s, set on a window scene ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and AppKit views find it up their responder chain ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"); a control’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks an event through the tracker found when its action fires, so each scene or window can have its own. Screen views can track themselves once a window scene or window turns it on with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreensAutomatically"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenViewed"},{"type":"text","text":" as each screen’s view controller appears, without swizzling ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and UIKit controls once a window scene turns it on with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackControlsAutomatically"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ControlActivated"},{"type":"text","text":" as a touch activates each control named by its accessibility identifier ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). On every platform, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackLifecycle"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and makes the tracker’s records durable as it leaves the foreground ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions"},{"type":"text","text":" enricher stamps every event with its session’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", a random identifier held in memory only, and starts a new session after a timeout of inactivity, tracking "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionEnded"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler"},{"type":"text","text":"s keeps a seeded fraction of the events they apply to, event by event, or whole sessions with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)"},{"type":"text","text":", dropping the rest on its worker before they are held, written or delivered, reporting each drop as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SamplingDropReport"},{"type":"text","text":" and stamping each kept record with its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SampleRateKey"},{"type":"text","text":". The standard enrichers, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.application()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"operatingSystem()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vendorIdentifier()"},{"type":"text","text":", stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale, network connection and the platform’s identifier for vendor, each under a typed key, the static ones read once ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" imports every module but "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", a product of its own for apps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that already use GRDB; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro derives an event’s conformances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and schema from its declaration and which alone builds swift-syntax; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exports those schemas as a JSON Schema tracking plan and checks the events against a committed one;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which runs that check from an app’s tests. Each module also has its own documentation and can be imported on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Traffluent","","struct SignedUp: Event {","    var plan: String","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople"]},{"anchor":"Modules","title":"Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting","doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"Traffluent","externalID":"Traffluent"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://Checksums/documentation/Checksums":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/checksums","kind":"symbol","title":"Checksums","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"},"doc://LoggingDestinations/documentation/LoggingDestinations":{"title":"LoggingDestinations","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/loggingdestinations"},"doc://AutomaticControlTracking/documentation/AutomaticControlTracking":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/automaticcontroltracking","kind":"symbol","title":"AutomaticControlTracking","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking"},"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking":{"title":"SwiftUITracking","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WhatGoesWhere":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Four signals, four jobs. Decide which one a fact belongs to before you write the line that records it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/whatgoeswhere","kind":"article","title":"Logging, Tracing, Metrics and Analytics","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere"},"doc://UIKitTracking/documentation/UIKitTracking":{"title":"UIKitTracking","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/uikittracking"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/events","kind":"symbol","title":"Events","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"title":"Trackers","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/trackers"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","kind":"symbol","title":"TracingDestinations","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"title":"Persistence","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence"},"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","kind":"symbol","title":"GRDBPersistence","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence"},"doc://Sessions/documentation/Sessions":{"title":"Sessions","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/sessions"},"doc://AutomaticScreenTracking/documentation/AutomaticScreenTracking":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking","kind":"symbol","title":"AutomaticScreenTracking","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking"},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"title":"EventMacros","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros"},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","kind":"symbol","title":"AppKitTracking","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/IdentifyingPeople":{"title":"Identifying People","kind":"article","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent knows people only by a pseudonymous session. An identifier that outlives one is yours to add, store, reset and gate with consent."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/identifyingpeople"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","kind":"symbol","title":"Traffluent","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"},"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"title":"Destinations","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/destinations"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","kind":"symbol","title":"TrackingPlans","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting":{"title":"DestinationTesting","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting"},"doc://StandardContext/documentation/StandardContext":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/standardcontext","kind":"symbol","title":"StandardContext","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"title":"HTTPDestinations","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations"},"doc://LifecycleTracking/documentation/LifecycleTracking":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/lifecycletracking","kind":"symbol","title":"LifecycleTracking","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"title":"TrackingPlanTesting","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting"}}}